{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Turkish financier Emre Tezmen \ndid not believe that anyone could  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5120,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "control the stock market. He told \nBloomberg this back in April, saying:  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9600,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"You cannot control anything 100% in a market. \nIf that were the case, prices would only go up.\"\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, that's a great point – but - for the \nbetter part of three years, prices at Tera,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22800,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his financial group, did only go up. Its \nflagship investment fund reported a return  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28800,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of more than sixty-six thousand percent over \nthree years, and that’s considered really good.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36720,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tera itself, a brokerage firm with around 130 \nemployees, was at times worth more than the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42640,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "global investment bank Lazard, which employs \nseveral thousand people. Which does seem a bit  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48640,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strange – but maybe his 130 employees were just \nmuch more productive than the slackers at Lazard.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, about five months after that \ninterview, everything fell apart.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61520,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turkey's capital markets regulator ordered the \nliquidation of 131 investment funds holding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68400,
    "dDurationMs": 8880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 20 billion dollars, and 455,758 people \nfound that their savings were locked inside.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77280,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turkey's justice minister has since described \nthe whole thing as a \"Ponzi-like scheme\"… which  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83600,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is never a good sign. And when a fund's returns \ndepend on a steady stream of new money coming in,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90800,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "its collapse is going to raise the question \nof who exactly was buying at the top.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96720,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, in this video, we'll look at \nhow the alleged scheme worked,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101120,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "why some Turkish money market funds (the product \npeople treat like cash) ended up holding the bag,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108000,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what Bill Hwang and Bernie Cornfeld have to \ndo with any of this, and what lessons the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113680,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rest of the world might want to take from it.\nMostly though, we are going to try to solve a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119680,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mystery. As his funds collapsed, Tezmen posted \na statement on social media blaming the whole  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126320,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing on a \"planned, deliberate and organized \nspeculative attack\" by \"notorious malevolent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133520,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forces\" (the worst kind of malevolent \nforces). That is a serious allegation,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I think we should take it seriously. Over \nthe course of this video, let's try to work  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144160,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out who these malevolent forces might be.\nIt would appear that Emre Tezmen was rarely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "troubled by self-doubt. He told \nBloomberg that his ambition was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154560,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to build \"the Goldman Sachs of Turkey.\"\nWe should note that Goldman Sachs took more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160160,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than 150 years to build, surviving several \nfinancial panics, and grew to employ tens of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166880,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thousands of people while building the reputation \nthat Matt Taibbi of Rolling Stone summed up as \"a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173600,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "great vampire squid wrapped around the face of \nhumanity.\" Tera was a lot younger and smaller,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180480,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it had recently signed a deal \nto sponsor the Turkish football  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 184880,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "club Beşiktaş… which is roughly the same thing.\nTezmen had a straightforward view of finance too.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"I make money, the investor makes money,\" \nhe told one interviewer. \"And what does the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196000,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state lose? There is no problem here.\" We'll \nhave to come back to that question later…\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202320,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, how did the Goldman Sachs of \nTurkey manage to so comprehensively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208000,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outperform the actual Goldman Sachs?\nWell, if you want a stock price to go up, you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "need buyers. And if you run an investment fund, \nthe most convenient buyer you can find is (of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220240,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "course) yourself… using your customers' money.\nBloomberg found regulatory filings showing that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227600,
    "dDurationMs": 9200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at one point in 2023, Tera's flagship fund had 99% \nof its assets in a single stock: shares of its own  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236800,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parent company, Tera. Most fund managers would \nconsider that a fairly concentrated position.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244720,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Orkun Saka, a lecturer at City St George's, \nUniversity of London, described how this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251040,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "works to Bloomberg back in April, before any \nof it had fallen apart. The fund's purchases,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257360,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he said, \"push up affiliated stock prices, which \ninflates the fund's net asset value, which makes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263760,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fund management business appear more valuable, \nwhich elevates the parent company's earnings and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270400,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stock price.\" As he put it: \"This loop is \nself-reinforcing by construction.\" That’s a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277120,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very academic way of describing a perpetual motion \nmachine. Turkey's justice minister later went with  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284160,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a less academic description: “Ponzi-like.”\nBefore I dig into how Tera kept that machine  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running, let me tell you about this week's \nvideo sponsor Saily. Mobile roaming is one  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296640,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the last industries still run \non the hotel minibar pricing model:  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the product is perfectly fine - but the price is \nrevealed later, and it's always considerably more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expensive than you expected. You land somewhere, \ncheck a map, send a few emails, and a month  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312480,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "later you discover that finding directions to \nyour hotel cost about as much as the hotel.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317840,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saily is an eSIM app that solves this problem. \nYou pick a prepaid data plan for wherever you're  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325360,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "going, and they offer affordable plans in \nover 200 destinations. Because it's prepaid,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331280,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you know exactly what you'll pay, so \nthere are no surprise roaming fees and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335840,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no angry calls to your phone company.\nWhat I like most is the convenience.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340880,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You install the Saily eSIM once, and that's it. \nThere's no need to install a new eSIM for every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347280,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "country you visit. You just choose a plan in \nthe app, and it activates automatically when  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352560,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you land. If anything does go wrong, their live \nchat support is available 24/7, which is useful  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358720,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when you're in a different time zone and your \nproblem doesn't care what time it is back home.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 364000,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Saily also blocks malicious sites, \ntrackers, and ads while you browse,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368480,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which has the pleasant side effect of saving you \ndata. They now offer app-based phone numbers too,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374880,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you can hand out a Saily number to shops and \ndelivery apps and keep your real one to yourself.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 380800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To get an exclusive 15% discount on \nSaily data plans, download the Saily  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386240,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "app and use code BOYLE at checkout, \nor click the link in the description.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391520,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, anyhow… a mild version of this happens \neverywhere. Academics call it \"portfolio  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 398160,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pumping.\" In a 2002 paper called \"Leaning for the \nTape,\" Carhart, Kaniel, Musto, and Reed showed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that some American mutual fund managers buy extra \nshares of stocks they already own at the very end  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412160,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the quarter, nudging up the closing prices \ntheir performance is measured on. The prices  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417920,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then drift back down the following morning.\nThe American version is worth a few basis points,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424960,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a few times a year, in time for the \nquarterly rankings. Tera's fund was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430960,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "buying the shares of its own affiliated \ncompanies all year round, and it reported  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 436560,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sixty-six thousand percent. Which just shows \nwhat you can achieve with a bit of ambition.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443760,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To keep a machine like this running, you need \na steady supply of new money, and in Turkey,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449760,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that wasn't hard to find. Inflation had averaged \nabout 50% a year for three years, eating away at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457200,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people's savings, so a fund reporting more than \n1,500% in a single year was going to get a lot  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 464720,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of attention. And when prices are rising 50% a \nyear, a big number on a fund statement probably  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471920,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "seems a bit less crazy than it would elsewhere. \nBack in 1998, the economists Sirri and Tufano  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480160,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "showed that investors pile into top-performing \nfunds far more eagerly than they pull money out  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486400,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of bad ones… and nobody was performing like Tera.\nTera's brokerage also took companies public (after  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 491600,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all they were trying to be the Goldman Sachs \nof Turkey) and its fund would then buy their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497120,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shares. Now, a small free float (the portion \nof a company's shares actually available to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503200,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trade) isn't unusual on its own. But when \nthe underwriter's own fund is one of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510000,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "main buyers of the few shares that do trade, \nit doesn't take much to move the price.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515520,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Take Vişne Madencilik, a mining company – that \nI’m fairly sure I mispronounced there - which Tera  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522400,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "took public in February 2025, putting 21% of its \nshares in public hands. By the end of July, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 530720,
    "dDurationMs": 8320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stock was up more than 2,100%. That same month, \nTera's fund and brokerage sold the shares they had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539040,
    "dDurationMs": 8640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bought in the IPO. In August, the stock fell 75%. \nThe Capital Markets Board fined two of Tera's fund  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547680,
    "dDurationMs": 9280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "managers 8.9 million lira each, about $199,000, \nfor creating a \"misleading perception on the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556960,
    "dDurationMs": 9200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "price, supply and demand\" of the shares. Keep the \nsize of that fine in mind. We'll need it later.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566160,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there was Destek Finans Faktoring, an \ninvoice factoring company Tera took public in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572720,
    "dDurationMs": 9120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "2025. Its shares rose more than 4,700%, making \nit Turkey's third-largest listed company. Even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581840,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the market turmoil started, it was still \ntrading at about 132 times earnings (JPMorgan  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 589040,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trades at about 15). And after the crash \nwiped about $4 billion off his paper fortune,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596400,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Destek's controlling shareholder, Altunç \nKumova, was left roughly as rich as the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600720,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "founder of Chobani yogurt. Invoice factoring is \na perfectly respectable business… but it doesn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 607120,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "usually produce Greek-yogurt levels of wealth. \nIt’s really just Greek yogurt that does that…\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Anyhow, back to our search for \nthe notorious malevolent forces.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 619760,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our first suspect is Ramazan Başak, the former \ndeputy head of MASAK, Turkey's financial crimes  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627120,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "agency. Mr. Başak says he repeatedly warned \nthe authorities about suspicious transactions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634080,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that his warnings were ignored. According to \nthe FT, he was detained in April for disseminating  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641200,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "misleading information in two social media \nposts, one of which questioned whether a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 646960,
    "dDurationMs": 8400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fund could really have returned 10,128%.\nWhich I suppose makes sense. If people start  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 655360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doubting ten-thousand-percent \nreturns, where does it end?\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 659840,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, Mr. Başak's attack consisted mainly of \nasking questions on social media, which isn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 666560,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "usually enough to bring down a 20-billion-dollar \nfund industry. So, we'll have to keep looking.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 673840,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How did Tera pay for all of this? A fund that \nkeeps buying its own affiliated stocks needs a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680800,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "steady supply of cash, and so Tera borrowed a lot \nof it. According to Bloomberg, its brokerage's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687440,
    "dDurationMs": 9536,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "borrowing went from 132 million lira at the end \nof 2024 to 59.8 billion lira a year later. That  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696976,
    "dDurationMs": 7344,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is about 450 times as much… in just a year...\nAnd a convenient place to find  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704320,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cash is in a money market fund.\nPeople think of money market funds as more or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710880,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "less the same as a bank account. They're supposed \nto hold boring, safe, liquid things – and earn an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717040,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "interest rate. But Bloomberg reports that some of \nthe firms at the center of this were lending money  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722960,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and taking hugely inflated stocks as collateral.\nThis type of loan is known as reverse repo – where  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730240,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fund makes a loan taking securities as \ncollateral, which it can sell if the borrower  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736000,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't pay it back. That should be very safe, as \nlong as the collateral is good - but in this case,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743040,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the collateral was pumped up shares \nin the thinly traded companies that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the affiliated funds were busy buying.\nIt’s a bit like taking a ten-dollar watch  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752960,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to a pawnbroker, explaining that it's actually \nworth ten thousand dollars because you just sold  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758400,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one to yourself for that price, and walking out \nwith a nine-thousand-dollar loan. And as Hilmi  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765600,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Güvenal points out on his Substack, the money \nmarket funds booked these loans at face value,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772000,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so their prices stayed perfectly stable… \nright up until the collateral had to be sold.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 778480,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this sounds familiar, it's because it’s \nsimilar to what Bill Hwang did at Archegos. Hwang  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784240,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "used swaps from global banks to build enormous \nleveraged positions in stocks like ViacomCBS.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791440,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Turkish funds did their borrowing at home, \nand financial experts who've looked at the trades  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 797120,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "say they borrowed against the inflated stocks \nthemselves. When Hwang's stocks fell in 2021,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804000,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "his banks made margin calls. When \nTera's prices stopped rising,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808880,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it faced a run from retail savers.\nBoth collapses happened very quickly,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815120,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and economists have a name for why this happens. \nBrunnermeier and Pedersen called it a 'liquidity  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 821680,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "spiral.' When prices fall, the collateral \nis worth less, so you can borrow less,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827360,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which forces you to sell, which pushes \nprices down further. And the faster you're  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832800,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forced to sell, the less anyone wants to pay.\nWhich brings us to our second suspect, and I feel  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840240,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we're getting closer… Bloomberg spoke to Mehmed \nKervanci, a 28-year-old who had put his savings  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847520,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into a high-flying Turkish stock fund to help \npay for his upcoming wedding. Two weeks later,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853600,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he was frantically hitting the sell button \non his phone's trading app. Another investor,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 858720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a 30-year-old trader, had put in the \ngold he received as wedding gifts,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 863440,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hoping to use it towards a deposit on a home.\nSo, it's possible that the planned, deliberate,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 869520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and organized speculative attack on Tera \nwas carried out by a 28-year-old trying  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 874800,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to pay for a wedding. But I don't want to jump to \nconclusions, so we should probably keep looking.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 881920,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you've pushed a stock up a few thousand \npercent, you only really make money if you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can sell it at that high price. And to sell \nat the top, you need someone who is willing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891520,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to buy at the top – which is really the \ncore question here. Who was buying?\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hilmi Güvenal, writing on his Substack, which I'll \nlink to in the description because it's one of the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902160,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clearest explanations of this whole mess that I've \nfound, points to one example: a shipbuilder called  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 908480,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Özata. According to its June financial statements, \nÖzata was losing money and had equity of around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915760,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "4.5 billion lira. By September, its share price \nhad reached 4,482 lira, giving it a market value  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924000,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of about 320 billion lira, or 71 times book \nvalue. Which is a lot for any shipbuilder… but  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 931600,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially so for a loss-making shipbuilder.\nAt that point, one of Tera's hedge funds  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 937680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "owned about 15% of the company. \nValued at the September price,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942480,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's roughly 48 billion lira of investors' \nmoney in a single loss-making shipyard.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949200,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turkey's capital markets regulator has \nsince filed criminal complaints against  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954640,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eleven people over trading in Özata shares.\nÖzata has also made its way into Turkish politics.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 962800,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "An opposition spokesman, Zeynel Emre, alleged \nthat a deputy chair of the ruling AK Party  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 968320,
    "dDurationMs": 8000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bought about 63 million lira of Özata shares in \nApril and sold them in September for about 1.34  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 976320,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion. He said the sales were completed before \nthe turmoil hit the stock market on September 16,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983120,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and he made similar claims about her husband. \nBloomberg notes that none of this has been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989520,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "independently confirmed. She stepped down \nfrom her party post, saying she wanted the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 995200,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "claims clarified \"without leaving any room for \ndoubt.\" She hasn't been charged with anything,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1001040,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and neither she nor her husband was among \nthe eleven people named by the regulator.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1007040,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To be clear, nobody has said who bought any \nof those shares. Güvenal notes that the answer  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1013680,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exists, since every trade is logged day by day. \nBut his broader point is the more important one.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1020160,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When a fund is one of the biggest buyers of \nan inflated stock, it can become the exit door  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025760,
    "dDurationMs": 8240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for anyone selling at the top… and the people \npaying for that exit are the fund's investors.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1034000,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Economists have a name for insiders moving money \nout at the expense of outside investors. In a 2000  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041200,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "paper, a group of researchers including the Nobel \nlaureate Simon Johnson called it “tunneling.” The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1048000,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "classic example is a controlling shareholder \nselling something to their own company at an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1054080,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inflated price: the insider gets the cash, and the \nminority shareholders pay for it. A fund can work  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1061520,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same way. If it pays an inflated price for \nshares, the seller walks away with real money, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fund's investors are left holding the bag.\nSo, how did a machine that was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1074080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running so smoothly seize up?\nOn August 29th, the Capital Markets Board,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1079680,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turkey's securities regulator, introduced a new \nrule capping how much of a company's free float  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086800,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single fund could hold. And as Hilmi Güvenal \npoints out, the rule was surprisingly gentle.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1094560,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Funds that were already over the limit were given \nuntil 2029 to comply, so nobody had to dump their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1102160,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shares. They just couldn't buy any more. And \na system that depends on somebody buying every  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1108960,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "single day has a problem when the buying stops.\nWhich brings us to our third suspect for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1115600,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the malevolent forces: the regulator.\nJohn Paul Rathbone of the FT said on the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121840,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unhedged podcast that the regulator had described \nsome of these fund prices as fictitious in an  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1128320,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "internal memo back in December. It then spent \neight months tightening things around the edges,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1135200,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when the big rule finally arrived, all \nit did was stop funds from adding to their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1140480,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positions. Which, it turns out, was enough.\nWith nobody left to keep buying, the prices had  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1148000,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nothing holding them up. In mid-September, \nTera announced that it was buying Pusula,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1153920,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another fund manager. The next day, Pusula \nsaid it couldn't meet redemption requests.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1161120,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This was not reassuring.\nInvestors pulled about 4.7  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1166720,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "billion dollars out of Turkish investment funds \nin just over two weeks, and on September 16th,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1173440,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tera said that it, too, was unable to \npay clients who wanted their money back.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1179280,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The football club Tera sponsored played its \nnext match without the Tera logo on its shirts,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1186160,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the club's own shares lost about \na third of their value that week.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1191200,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I would have expected the lack of writing on their \nshirts to be viewed positively – but I guess they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1196960,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "probably needed the sponsorship money.\nRuns like this tend to feed on themselves,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1202800,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there's a good reason for that. If you have \nto sell your house in the next hour instead of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208080,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the next month, you're going to have to cut the \nprice, however nice the house is. A fund facing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1215200,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a wave of redemptions has the same problem. It \npays the first people out by selling whatever  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1221440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is easiest to sell, and the people who stay \nare left owning the thinly traded stocks,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227200,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which can only be sold in a hurry at a discount.\nA well-known 2010 study of American mutual funds  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1235040,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "found exactly this: funds holding illiquid \nassets see much bigger outflows after bad news,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1242400,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because investors understand that waiting costs \nthem. So, the people rushing for the exit that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1249760,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "week were being shrewd. The ones who waited were \nthe ones who ended up paying for the discount.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1257600,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For the people who didn't get out in time, the \nresults have been devastating. One investor told  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1263600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bloomberg that he had moved 2.4 million lira out \nof gold and into two Tera equity funds at the end  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1269200,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of August. \"My nerves are wrecked,\" he said. \n\"I can't sleep.\" And as an entrepreneur who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274880,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lost 90% of his investment in Pusula funds put \nit: \"These were all regulator-approved funds.\"\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1282000,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How did this go on for so long? Well, as Robert \nArmstrong put it on the FT's Unhedged podcast, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1289440,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problems were something of an open secret – quite \na lot of people could see what was going on.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1295040,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In February 2025, Istanbul's chief prosecutor \nwrote to the capital markets regulator asking  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1302480,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it to look into unusual share trading by \nthe chairman of Pusula. In November 2025,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1309040,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Turkey's finance minister publicly stated that \nthe government knew stock price manipulation was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1314800,
    "dDurationMs": 8800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "taking place through certain funds. In June 2026, \nMSCI warned about \"recurring instances of possible  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1323600,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "coordinated trading behavior.\" And yet, the big \nrule change didn't come until the end of August.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1330640,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Part of the reason this went on for so long may \nbe that getting caught just wasn't very expensive.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1337840,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The economist Gary Becker, who later won a Nobel \nPrize, argued back in 1968 that criminals approach  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1345280,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crime much like the way businessmen approach any \nother business decision – they weigh the expected  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1351920,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gains against the chance of getting caught, \nmultiplied by the penalty. If stock market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1357600,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manipulation can make you hundreds of millions of \ndollars, and the fine if you get caught is just  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1364000,
    "dDurationMs": 8640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "$199,000, the math is not very complicated. A \nfine like that is just a small operating expense.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1372640,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Deterrence needs more than just fines. In 2001, \nthe legal scholar Bernard Black analyzed the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1380240,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "institutions a country needs to have strong stock \nmarkets. His list includes an honest regulator,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1387200,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "independent courts, auditors that can be held \nliable, and a free press. Turkey has all of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1394400,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these on paper. In practice, as the Economist has \nnoted, officials were slow to act on the warnings,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1401440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the former financial crimes official \nwe met earlier says he was detained  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1405920,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "twice after raising concerns about Tera, and \nTera threatened to sue reporters and social  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1412000,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "media users who accused it of wrongdoing.\nWhen people don't trust the institutions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1418400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they often rely on connections instead. As the \nFT noted, the boards of companies caught up in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1425200,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the scandal included a former ambassador \nto the OECD and a university rector,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1431440,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and Tera's financial holding company was run \nby a former deputy governor of the central  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1436960,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "bank. Americans may remember that Theranos had two \nformer secretaries of state on its board – Henry  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1443920,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kissinger and George Shultz – which was comforting \nto investors, even if neither of them had any  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1449600,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "background in science or blood testing.\nIn a famous 2001 paper, the economist  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1455680,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Raymond Fisman put a number on this sort of \nthing. He looked at Indonesia under Suharto  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1462320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and found that whenever rumors spread about \nSuharto's health, the shares of companies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1467760,
    "dDurationMs": 7200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "closely connected to him fell much further than \nthose of less well-connected firms. Connections  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1474960,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can be very valuable… for as long as they last.\nOur fourth suspect for the notorious malevolent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1482640,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "forces has to be MSCI, a foreign \nindex provider based in New York.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1488960,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Turkish government has spent years promoting \nIstanbul as a global financial center, so I  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1495760,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "imagine they were excited to read MSCI's June 2026 \nMarket Classification Review. It opened with good  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1503600,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "news for Bulgaria, which is being promoted up to \nFrontier Market status, and closed with a reminder  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1510560,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that Greece is being promoted to Developed Market \nstatus. In between, it warned Turkey and Indonesia  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1517680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about coordinated trading activity on their stock \nmarkets. Turkey was told that MSCI \"may launch  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1524560,
    "dDurationMs": 7840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a consultation on the appropriate treatment for \nTurkey,\" which is probably not a positive review.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1532400,
    "dDurationMs": 7120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As the Economist read it, Turkey was being warned \nthat it might pass Bulgaria on the way down,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1539520,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and S\u0026P Dow Jones has since put Turkey \nunder review for exactly that downgrade.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1545360,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They point out that frontier status would \nput Turkey in the same category as much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1551200,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller markets like Tunisia and Romania.\nThis isn't what you want to hear when you're  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1558480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "trying to build a global financial center, and \nJohn Paul Rathbone suggested on the Unhedged  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1564160,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "podcast that the threat of a downgrade in \nNovember was probably what finally pushed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1569680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the regulator to act. So, MSCI may have set the \nwhole thing in motion, although calling a press  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1576560,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "release a speculative attack does seem like a \nbit of a stretch. Still, we should probably keep  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1582640,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them on our list of suspects – the alternative \nwould be to start looking at the people who were  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1587760,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "running the funds, and that hardly seems fair.\nIt would be easy to assume that a scandal like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1593920,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this only affects the people who lost \nmoney in the funds, but unfortunately,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1599520,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the damage spreads a lot further than that.\nBack in 1970, the economist George Akerlof,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1606320,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who later won a Nobel Prize, explained why \ndishonesty is so harmful, using the market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1612320,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for used cars as an example. When buyers \ncan't tell the good cars from the bad ones,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1618400,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "(the \"lemons,\") they'll only pay an average price \nfor a used car. So, the owners of good cars stop  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1626080,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selling, and the market fills up with lemons.\nTurkish stocks now have a “market for lemons”  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1632880,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "problem. Turkey's finance minister has been \ntrying to get companies to raise money on the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1638640,
    "dDurationMs": 8160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "stock market rather than relying on expensive bank \nloans, and it was working. According to the FT, 34  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1646800,
    "dDurationMs": 7920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies raised 82.4 billion lira through IPOs in \nthe first eight months of this year, far more than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1654720,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in all of 2025. But if investors can't tell which \nsmall companies are good businesses and which are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1662320,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "propped up by a friendly fund, they'll either stay \naway from the stock market altogether - or demand  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1668640,
    "dDurationMs": 9280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a discount on all of them. Honest companies end up \npaying a higher cost of capital. This scandal also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1677920,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hits Turkish asset managers - a recent working \npaper found that money was already leaving  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1684240,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "independent fund managers with no connection to \nthe scandal and heading for funds owned by banks.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1691760,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "None of this is uniquely Turkish, of course. \nFinancial history is mostly just different  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1697680,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people discovering the same trick a few \ndecades apart and calling it innovation.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1703440,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the 1960s, Bernie Cornfeld, who happened \nto have been born in Istanbul, built Investors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1710160,
    "dDurationMs": 6293,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Overseas Services into one of the biggest fund \nbusinesses in the world, selling funds door to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1716453,
    "dDurationMs": 7307,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "door across Europe. His famous recruiting line was \n\"Do you sincerely want to be rich?\", a question to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1723760,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which most people answer – I sincerely do...\nOne of his funds owned oil and gas exploration  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1731040,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "permits in the Canadian Arctic, which it \nhad bought from an oilman named John King.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1736880,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to a later US court ruling, in \nDecember 1969 King arranged the sale of a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1743680,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "small slice of his own group's Arctic permits \nat a much higher price, and that same night,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1749600,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a Friday, the fund used that price to revalue \nits entire holding upward. A few weeks later,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1756320,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the fund effectively reimbursed King by selling \nhim an identical slice on the same terms. It was  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1763280,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same trick: a tiny trade, a big revaluation, \nand a price that nobody could actually sell at.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1770560,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Most American savers avoided all of this \nfor a fairly boring reason. Back in 1967,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1777600,
    "dDurationMs": 8880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the SEC had forced IOS to stop selling its funds \nto Americans. The institutions did their job.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1786480,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then there's Bill Hwang. His lawyers argued that \nbuying shares on the open market, at whatever  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1793440,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "price the market is offering, can't be illegal \nmanipulation. It's an idea legal scholars have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1800320,
    "dDurationMs": 7600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debated for decades. A jury in New York disagreed, \nand in 2024 Hwang was convicted of fraud, market  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1807920,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manipulation, and racketeering, and sentenced \nto eighteen years in prison. He's free on bail  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1813920,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while he appeals, and according to Bloomberg, \nhe has also applied for a presidential pardon.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1820080,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What can the rest of the \nworld take from all this?\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1824960,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Be wary of any price that's mostly set by \nthe people who already own large positions  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1830480,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the asset. Whether it's a company that keeps \nraising money to buy more of the same thing,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1836000,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or a hot new stock where only a few percent of \nthe shares ever trade, the price on the screen  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1842160,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can tell you very little about what the asset \nwould be worth if it traded freely in a deep,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1848800,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "liquid market. And when bad actors can pump stocks \nwithout paying much of a price, honest businesses  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1855520,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "eventually stop trying to compete.\nSo, where do things stand now?\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1861360,
    "dDurationMs": 7360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "According to Turkey's justice minister, 217 \nsuspects have been targeted in the probe so far,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1868720,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and 56 people have been jailed pending trial. \nThe capital markets regulator has given İşbank  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1875440,
    "dDurationMs": 7520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the state-run Ziraat Bank up to six \nmonths to liquidate the 131 frozen funds.\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1882960,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as Hilmi Güvenal points out, anyone whose \nsell order was cancelled when the funds were  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1889280,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "frozen is no longer owed money. They're simply \nentitled to their share of whatever the banks  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1895440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manage to raise. And when you try to sell \nbillions of lira of inflated factoring  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1900320,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies and loss-making shipyards all at \nonce, you run into problems. Murat Gulkan,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1906880,
    "dDurationMs": 7680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the CEO of OMG Capital Advisors, estimates that \nthe assets would fetch \"pennies on the dollar.\"\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1914560,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, who is stepping in as the buyer of last \nresort? Well, the Turkish sovereign wealth  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1920960,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fund has reportedly been buying blue-chip \nstocks to prevent the wider market from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1926240,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "crashing. A state-owned Islamic bank is in talks \nto take over two savings-finance companies from  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1933200,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Pusula group. The deposit insurance fund is \nset to receive any assets the courts decide are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1940000,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the proceeds of crime. And the country's \nvice president has been put in charge of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1945440,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a council overseeing the whole liquidation.\nWhich brings us back to Emre Tezmen's philosophy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1951920,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of finance: \"I make money, the investor \nmakes money. And what does the state lose?\"\n "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1958000,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It appears the state is now finding out.\nAnd it also brings us to the end of our  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1964560,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "search for the notorious malevolent forces. \nAfter ruling out whistleblowers, regulators,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1970560,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "New York index providers, and 28-year-olds \ntrying to pay for a wedding, we finally have  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1976320,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our answer. The planned, deliberate, and organized \nspeculative attack that brought down the Goldman  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1982480,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sachs of Turkey was carried out by sellers.\nTezmen had built a perfect financial machine.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1989760,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Its only design flaw was that it \nrequired an economy in which absolutely  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1994800,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nobody ever pressed the sell button.\nIf you found this video interesting,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1999600,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you should watch my video on the crypto \ninfinite money glitch next. Don’t forget to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2004560,
    "dDurationMs": 7760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "check out our sponsor Saily using the link in the \ndescription and see you in the next video, bye."
    } ]
  } ]
}
